1. Requirements
===============
- USE (downloads available here: http://sourceforge.net/projects/useocl/)

2. Installation
===============
Please, copy the jar-file into the lib/plugins directory of USE.

The Java based solver SAT4j comes with the plugin and needs no installation.

Native solvers are installed by hand. Copy a solver's library into
lib/plugins/modelValidatorPlugin/x64 under the USE directory, or into
lib/plugins/modelValidatorPlugin/x86 for a 32-bit Java. The plugin adds that
folder to the library path when it starts. Name the library after the solver,
in lower case: libminisat.so on Linux or minisat.dll on Windows for MiniSat,
and likewise for lingeling, minisatprover and cryptominisat. The plingeling
solver is an executable named plingeling in the same folder. Then select the
solver with `mv -config satsolver:=MiniSat'. When the plugin cannot load the
solver, the command lists the solvers it can load.

3. Usage
===============
The shell command 'plugins' shows all available Model Validator commands.
For further information, please feel free to use our sourceforge forums. A
quick reference guide is included in the Model Validator ZIP archive.